            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for to honour, then the Malayalam for to make one's own."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: രാജാവ്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "രാജാവ് — rājāvŭ — \"a king\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പണ്ടുപണ്ട് ഒരു രാജ്യത്ത് ഒരു നല്ല രാജാവ് ഉണ്ടായിരുന്നു. paṇṭupaṇṭŭ oru rājyattŭ oru nalla rājāvŭ uṇṭāyirunnu. Once upon a time there was a good king in a country."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: രാജാക്കന്മാർ, rājākkanmār."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural രാജാക്കന്മാർ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "രാജാവ് (rājāvŭ) is borrowed from Sanskrit rājan, \"a chieftain, a king\" (CDIAL 10679), the root of രാജ്യം (rājyaṁ), \"a country, a kingdom\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
